    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR fixes correctness and performance issues in the IDL “reachable functions” analysis by improving caching behavior, adding recursion handling, and extending test coverage to lock in the intended reachability semantics.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Update `reachable_functions` to cache full transitive results per call-site key (instead of a boolean sentinel) and use a composite key rather than `.hash`.\n- Add `SystemStackError` handling during reachability evaluation and thread a shared cache through instruction reachability collection.\n- Add a dedicated reachable-functions test suite covering direct/transitive calls, branching behavior, builtins, deduplication, recursion/shared-cache behavior.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 4 out of 5 changed files in this pull request and generated 5 comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/obj/instruction.rb | Adds a cache parameter to instruction-level reachable-functions traversal and forwards it into the IDL AST pass. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/cfg_arch.rb | Uses a shared cache across instruction traversal and fixes memoization collisions for condition builders. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/sorbet/rbi/gems/udb@0.1.0.rbi | Updates RBI signature to match the new `reachable_functions(effective_xlen, cache=...)` API shape. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/idlc/test/test_functions.rb | Adds a new `TestReachableFunctions` suite plus compilation helpers. |\r\n| tools/ruby-gems/idlc/lib/idlc/passes/reachable_functions.rb | Fixes cache keying/caching semantics and rescues `SystemStackError` as a type error. |\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Files not reviewed (1)</summary>\n\n* **tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/sorbet/rbi/gems/udb@0.1.0.rbi**: Language not supported\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Comments suppressed due to low confidence (1)</summary>\n\n**tools/ruby-gems/udb/lib/udb/obj/instruction.rb:503**\n* The memoization type for `@memo.reachable_functions` is inconsistent with what is stored: the hash values are arrays returned by `ast.reachable_functions(...)`, not a single `Idl::FunctionDefAst`. Update the `T.let` type to `T::Hash[Integer, T::Array[Idl::FunctionDefAst]]` (or similar) so Sorbet reflects reality.\n```\n      else\n        @memo.reachable_functions ||= T.let({}, T::Hash[Integer, Idl::FunctionDefAst])\n        @memo.reachable_functions[effective_xlen] ||=\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-unified-db/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
